content:
{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "FIELD GUIDE FG-07 · 2ND EDITION"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "The Spares Cataloguer's Field Guide"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "How to write MRO spares and consumables data so that everyone finds the same part."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Inside"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "• 8 golden rules you can learn over a coffee"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "• 10 chapters: bearings, seals, O-rings, belts, oils, greases, filters, bolts, hoses and gloves"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "• Before / after examples for every field"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "• FAQ, checklist and lookup tables"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Published by the Materials Cataloguing Team · October 2026 · Sample document for system testing"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Hi, cataloguer!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "You're the person who decides whether the warehouse holds one bin of 6205-2RS/C3 bearings or five bins of the same bearing under five different names. This guide is here to make that decision easy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Each record you work on arrives as rows with three columns: Item, Attribute and Value. In this guide we call the item a category (what kind of thing it is) and the attribute a field (one fact about it). You'll translate each row into the guide's words and write it back in the same three columns, in the same order. If your tool has a fourth column for notes, list the rule codes you used - for example GR2; BRG-1."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "How this guide is organised"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Part",
        "What you'll find",
        "Use it when"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "Part": "Golden rules (GR1-GR8)",
          "What you'll find": "Eight rules that apply everywhere",
          "Use it when": "Always - they're the default"
        },
        {
          "Part": "Cheat sheet",
          "What you'll find": "Unit conversions on one page",
          "Use it when": "You see inches, psi, gallons, pounds"
        },
        {
          "Part": "Chapters 1-10",
          "What you'll find": "One per category: fields at a glance, rule cards, before/after",
          "Use it when": "You're working on that category"
        },
        {
          "Part": "FAQ",
          "What you'll find": "The questions everyone asks in week one",
          "Use it when": "You're unsure and nobody's around"
        },
        {
          "Part": "Lookup tables",
          "What you'll find": "AS568 sizes, dash sizes, UNC threads, V-belt offsets",
          "Use it when": "A rule card tells you to look something up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Words we use"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Word",
        "Meaning"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "Word": "Category",
          "Meaning": "The kind of item, e.g. Rolling Bearing. Written in the Item column, Title Case."
        },
        {
          "Word": "Field",
          "Meaning": "One fact about the item, e.g. bore_diameter. Written in the Attribute column as a lower_snake_case key."
        },
        {
          "Word": "Value",
          "Meaning": "The fact itself, e.g. 25 mm. Written in the Value column."
        },
        {
          "Word": "Picklist",
          "Meaning": "A closed list of allowed values. If a field has one, the value must come from it."
        },
        {
          "Word": "Rule card",
          "Meaning": "A small box in each chapter telling you, in IF / THEN form, how to turn messy input into a clean value."
        },
        {
          "Word": "TBD / CHECK:",
          "Meaning": "Your two safety valves: TBD when the value is missing, CHECK: when it can't be mapped."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The order of work. 1) Tidy spaces. 2) Missing? write TBD. 3) Fix the category (GR1). 4) Fix the field key (GR2). 5) Apply the chapter's rule card. 6) Convert units (GR5) and tidy numbers (GR4). 7) Still doesn't fit? CHECK: (GR7)."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "The 8 golden rules"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Learn these and you'll get 80 % of rows right without opening a chapter."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "GR1 Use the category name from this guide"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Every row starts with a category. Write it exactly as the chapter title, in Title Case: Rolling Bearing, O-Ring, Hex Bolt. Nicknames like Brg, Oring or Hyd Hose are fine to receive - just never to write."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "Brg",
          "AFTER": "Rolling Bearing"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "Hyd Hose",
          "AFTER": "Hydraulic Hose"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "GR2 Field keys are lower_snake_case"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The attribute column holds a field key, not a label. Keys are lower case with underscores, exactly as listed in each chapter's 'Fields at a glance' table. Labels such as 'Shaft Dia' or 'Pack Size' are translated into the key."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "Shaft Dia",
          "AFTER": "shaft_diameter"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "Part No",
          "AFTER": "designation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "GR3 Picklist values are spelled exactly like the guide"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If a field has a picklist, copy the value character for character: words in Title Case, acronyms in capitals, symbols kept (Deep Groove Ball, Lithium Complex, SiC/Carbon, JIC 37° Female Swivel)."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "deep groove",
          "AFTER": "Deep Groove Ball"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "li complex",
          "AFTER": "Lithium Complex"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "GR4 Numbers: metric, one space, short and tidy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Measured values are metric: number, one space, unit (25 mm, 10.3 bar, 208 L). Use at most one decimal and drop trailing zeros (70 mm, not 70.0 mm). The only exception is O-ring dimensions, which always carry two decimals (3.53 mm, 25.00 mm)."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "25mm",
          "AFTER": "25 mm"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "70 .0 mm",
          "AFTER": "70 mm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "GR5 Convert imperial units - don't keep both"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Inches, pounds, gallons, psi and ounces are converted with the cheat sheet on page 4. Write only the metric result; never '50.8 mm (2 in)'"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "2 in",
          "AFTER": "50.8 mm"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "150 psid",
          "AFTER": "10.3 bar"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "GR6 Don't know? Write TBD"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Empty cells, dashes, n/a, ?, 'unknown', 'see drawing' all become TBD (capitals). Never guess - a TBD gets fixed, a guess gets bought."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "n/a",
          "AFTER": "TBD"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "?",
          "AFTER": "TBD"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "GR7 Can't map it? Flag it with CHECK:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If a value doesn't fit the field's picklist or format even after every rule in its chapter, write CHECK: followed by a space and the original text. A reviewer will pick it up."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "semi-synthetic",
          "AFTER": "CHECK: semi-synthetic"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "level 5",
          "AFTER": "CHECK: level 5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "GR8 One row in, one row out"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Never split one row into several or merge rows together. Keep the order of the file. If a value carries information for another field (like 'EP2' for a grease), use only the part that belongs to this row's field."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BEFORE": "EP2 (for nlgi_grade)",
          "AFTER": "NLGI 2"
        },
        {
          "BEFORE": "EP2 (for ep_additive)",
          "AFTER": "Yes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Cheat sheet: units"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Multiply, then round as the field says. If the chapter has a standard-pack or lookup table, that wins over the plain conversion."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "If you see",
        "Write in",
        "Do this"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "If you see": "inch (in, \")",
          "Write in": "mm",
          "Do this": "x 25.4"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "foot (ft, \')",
          "Write in": "m",
          "Do this": "x 0.3048"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "psi / psid / psig",
          "Write in": "bar",
          "Do this": "x 0.0689476"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "MPa",
          "Write in": "bar",
          "Do this": "x 10"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "US gallon (gal)",
          "Write in": "L",
          "Do this": "x 3.785"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "US quart (qt)",
          "Write in": "L",
          "Do this": "x 0.946"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "pound (lb)",
          "Write in": "kg",
          "Do this": "x 0.4536"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "ounce (oz)",
          "Write in": "kg",
          "Do this": "x 0.02835"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "gram (g)",
          "Write in": "kg",
          "Do this": "/ 1000"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "metre (m)",
          "Write in": "mm",
          "Do this": "x 1000 (lengths of belts, hoses, gloves)"
        },
        {
          "If you see": "°F",
          "Write in": "°C",
          "Do this": "(F - 32) / 1.8"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Rounding. Round half up. 15.876 kg becomes 15.9 kg; 344.7 bar becomes 345 bar when the field asks for whole numbers; 24.9936 mm becomes 24.99 mm for O-rings."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Rolling Bearing"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Bearings are the most duplicated items in any spares catalogue, because every manufacturer adds its own suffixes to the same basic part. Your job is to strip the brand dialect and leave a designation any store-person can match on the shelf."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Write the category as: Rolling Bearing  You may receive: Bearing; Ball Bearing; Roller Bearing; Brg; Deep Groove Ball Bearing; Anti-friction Bearing"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Fields at a glance"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Rule",
        "Field key",
        "Labels you may see",
        "What to write"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BRG-1": "designation",
          "Labels you may see": "Designation; Part No; Bearing No; Bearing Number; Code",
          "What to write": "Base number, then -seal, then /clearance: 6205-2RS/C3"
        },
        {
          "BRG-2": "bearing_type",
          "Labels you may see": "Type; Bearing Type",
          "What to write": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "BRG-3": "bore_diameter",
          "Labels you may see": "Bore; ID; Inner Diameter; d",
          "What to write": "{n} mm"
        },
        {
          "BRG-4": "outside_diameter",
          "Labels you may see": "OD; Outer Diameter; D",
          "What to write": "{n} mm"
        },
        {
          "BRG-5": "width",
          "Labels you may see": "Width; B; Thickness",
          "What to write": "{n} mm"
        },
        {
          "BRG-6": "seal_type",
          "Labels you may see": "Seals; Seal; Shields; Closure",
          "What to write": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "BRG-7": "internal_clearance",
          "Labels you may see": "Clearance; Internal Clearance; Radial Clearance",
          "What to write": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "BRG-8": "cage_material",
          "Labels you may see": "Cage; Cage Material; Retainer",
          "What to write": "Picklist value"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Rule cards"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "BRG-1 designation\nIF seal suffix IN (2RS1, 2RSH, 2RSR, LLU, DDU, 2RS) THEN write -2RS\nIF seal suffix IN (ZZ, 2ZR, 2Z, ZZC) THEN write -2Z\nIF clearance suffix present (C2, C3, C4, C5) THEN append /Cn at the end\nREMOVE spaces, dots and extra hyphens between the parts; REMOVE cage codes (M, MA, J, TN9) - they go to cage_material\nWatch out! Don't 'upgrade' a bearing: 6205 and 6205-2RS are different parts. Only translate what is written."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "BRG-2 bearing_type\nIF value IN (DGBB; deep groove; radial ball) THEN write \"Deep Groove Ball\"\nIF value IN (ACBB; angular contact) THEN write \"Angular Contact Ball\"\nIF value IN (CRB; cylindrical) THEN write \"Cylindrical Roller\"\nIF value IN (SRB; spherical; self-aligning roller) THEN write \"Spherical Roller\"\nIF value IN (TRB; taper; tapered) THEN write \"Tapered Roller\"\nIF value IN (thrust) THEN write \"Thrust Ball\"\nIF value IN (self-aligning ball) THEN write \"Self-Aligning Ball\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "BRG-3 bore_diameter\nIF unit is inch THEN multiply by 25.4\nIF no unit THEN assume mm (bearing catalogues are metric)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "BRG-4 outside_diameter\nSame as bore_diameter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "FG-07 · The Spares Cataloguer's Field Guide"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "2nd edition"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "BRG-5 width"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Same as bore_diameter"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "BRG-6 seal_type"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (rubber seals both sides; 2RS1; LLU; sealed both sides) THEN write \"2RS\"\nIF value IN (metal shields; shielded both sides; ZZ) THEN write \"2Z\"\nIF value IN (one rubber seal; RS1) THEN write \"RS\"\nIF value IN (one shield) THEN write \"Z\"\nIF value IN (open; no seals) THEN write \"Open\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "BRG-7 internal_clearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (C2; less than normal) THEN write \"C2\"\nIF value IN (normal; CN; standard) THEN write \"CN\"\nIF value IN (C3; C 3; greater than normal) THEN write \"C3\"\nIF value IN (C4) THEN write \"C4\"\nIF value IN (C5) THEN write \"C5\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "BRG-8 cage_material"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (J; pressed steel; steel) THEN write \"Steel\"\nIF value IN (M; MA; machined brass; brass) THEN write \"Brass\"\nIF value IN (TN9; TN; nylon; PA66; polyamide) THEN write \"Polyamide\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Before → after"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "Part No: 6205 2RS1 C3": "designation: 6205-2RS/C3"
        },
        {
          "Designation: 6205ZZ": "designation: 6205-ZZ"
        },
        {
          "Bearing No: 6310-2RSR-C3": "designation: 6310-2RS/C3"
        },
        {
          "Type: DGBB": "bearing_type: Deep Groove Ball"
        },
        {
          "Bearing Type: spherical": "bearing_type: Spherical Roller"
        },
        {
          "Type: taper": "bearing_type: Tapered Roller"
        },
        {
          "Bore: 1 in": "bore_diameter: 25.4 mm"
        },
        {
          "ID: 25mm": "bore_diameter: 25 mm"
        },
        {
          "OD: 52": "outside_diameter: 52 mm"
        },
        {
          "Seals: metal shields": "seal_type: 2Z"
        },
        {
          "Clearance: normal": "internal_clearance: CN"
        },
        {
          "Cage: TN9": "cage_material: Polyamide"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Pro tip. Bore code shortcut: for series 6000-6300 with bore code 04 and up, bore = code x 5 mm (6205 -> 25 mm). Use it to sanity-check, not to fill blanks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "6"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Mechanical Seal"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Mechanical seals follow API 682, so most of the vocabulary is already standard - it's just written fifteen different ways. Stick to the API words and you're done."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Write the category as: Mechanical Seal  You may receive: Mech Seal; Mechanical Seal; Pump Seal; Cartridge Seal"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Fields at a glance"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Rule",
        "Field key",
        "Labels you may see",
        "What to write"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "MSL-1": "arrangement",
          "Arrangement; Config; Configuration": "Arrangement 1 | 2 | 3"
        },
        {
          "MSL-2": "seal_category",
          "Category; Cat; API Category": "Category 1 | 2 | 3"
        },
        {
          "MSL-3": "seal_type",
          "Seal Type; Type; Design": "Type A | B | C"
        },
        {
          "MSL-4": "shaft_diameter",
          "Shaft Size; Shaft Dia; Sleeve Size; Shaft": "{n} mm"
        },
        {
          "MSL-5": "face_combination",
          "Faces; Face Materials; Face Combination": "{rotating}/{stationary}"
        },
        {
          "MSL-6": "secondary_seal",
          "Elastomer; Secondary Seal; O-rings": "Picklist value (same as O-Ring material)"
        },
        {
          "MSL-7": "flush_plan",
          "Flush Plan; API Plan; Piping Plan": "Plan {code}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Rule cards"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "MSL-1 arrangement\nIF value IN (single; single seal) THEN write \"Arrangement 1\"\nIF value IN (tandem; dual unpressurized; dual unpressurised) THEN write \"Arrangement 2\"\nIF value IN (double; dual pressurized; double pressurized; back-to-back) THEN write \"Arrangement 3\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "MSL-2 seal_category\nIF value matches cat 1/2/3 in any spelling (CAT2, Cat. 2) THEN write Category n"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "MSL-3 seal_type\nIF value IN (pusher; O-ring pusher; rotating pusher) THEN write \"Type A\"\nIF value IN (metal bellows; low temperature bellows) THEN write \"Type B\"\nIF value IN (high temperature metal bellows; flexible graphite bellows) THEN write \"Type C\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "MSL-4 shaft_diameter\nREMOVE the diameter sign Ø\nIF unit is inch THEN multiply by 25.4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "MSL-5 face_combination\nIF value IN (carbon; carbon graphite; antimony carbon) THEN write \"Carbon\"\nIF value IN (silicon carbide; SSiC; RBSiC; SiC) THEN write \"SiC\"\nIF value IN (tungsten carbide; WC; TC) THEN write \"TC\"\nTranslate each face with the picklist, keep the order given, join with / (no spaces)\nSeparators vs, v, against, - , / all mean the same"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "MSL-6 secondary_seal"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (nitrile; Buna-N; Buna) THEN write \"NBR\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (hydrogenated nitrile; HSN) THEN write \"HNBR\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (Viton; fluorocarbon; FPM) THEN write \"FKM\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (Kalrez; perfluoroelastomer; perfluoro) THEN write \"FFKM\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (EPR; ethylene propylene) THEN write \"EPDM\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (silicone; Si) THEN write \"VMQ\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (Aflas; TFE/P) THEN write \"FEPM\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "MSL-7 flush_plan"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Write Plan, one space, the plan number, suffix letter in capitals: Plan 53A"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Combined plans joined with /: Plan 11/52"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Before → after"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "Arrangement: tandem": "arrangement: Arrangement 2"
        },
        {
          "Config: double pressurized": "arrangement: Arrangement 3"
        },
        {
          "Category: CAT2": "seal_category: Category 2"
        },
        {
          "Seal Type: metal bellows": "seal_type: Type B"
        },
        {
          "Shaft Size: 2.5 in": "shaft_diameter: 63.5 mm"
        },
        {
          "Shaft Dia: Ø60": "shaft_diameter: 60 mm"
        },
        {
          "Faces: SiC vs carbon": "face_combination: SiC/Carbon"
        },
        {
          "Face Materials: tungsten carbide / silicon carbide": "face_combination: TC/SiC"
        },
        {
          "Elastomer: Viton": "secondary_seal: FKM"
        },
        {
