        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "CHAPTER 3 · CODE ORG"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "O-Ring"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "O-rings are cheap, but a wrong one stops a compressor. The two things that matter are size and compound. Note the special rule: O-ring dimensions always have two decimals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Write the category as: O-Ring  You may receive: O-ring; Oring; O Ring; Seal Ring; Toroidal Seal"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Fields at a glance"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Rule",
        "Field key",
        "Labels you may see",
        "What to write"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "Rule": "ORG-1",
          "Field key": "size_reference",
          "Labels you may see": "Size; Dash No; Dash Number; AS568",
          "What to write": "AS568-{nnn}"
        },
        {
          "Rule": "ORG-2",
          "Field key": "inner_diameter",
          "Labels you may see": "ID; Inner Diameter; Inside Diameter",
          "What to write": "{n.nn} mm (two decimals!)"
        },
        {
          "Rule": "ORG-3",
          "Field key": "cross_section",
          "Labels you may see": "CS; Cross Section; Section; W",
          "What to write": "{n.nn} mm (two decimals!)"
        },
        {
          "Rule": "ORG-4",
          "Field key": "material",
          "Labels you may see": "Material; Compound; Elastomer",
          "What to write": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "Rule": "ORG-5",
          "Field key": "hardness",
          "Labels you may see": "Hardness; Durometer; Shore",
          "What to write": "{n} Shore A"
        },
        {
          "Rule": "ORG-6",
          "Field key": "aed_resistant",
          "Labels you may see": "RGD; AED; Explosive Decompression; ED Resistant",
          "What to write": "Yes | No"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Rule cards"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ORG-1 size_reference\nIF value is a 3-digit dash number with or without prefix (214, -214, 2-214, AS 568-214) THEN write AS568-214\nThe leading '2-' used by some suppliers is a compound prefix, not part of the size"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ORG-2 inner_diameter\nIF inch THEN x 25.4\nALWAYS two decimals: 25.00 mm"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ORG-3 cross_section\nDecimal comma becomes point: 3,53 -> 3.53 mm"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ORG-4 material\nIF value IN (nitrile; Buna-N; Buna) THEN write \"NBR\"\nIF value IN (hydrogenated nitrile; HSN) THEN write \"HNBR\"\nIF value IN (Viton; fluorocarbon; FPM) THEN write \"FKM\"\nIF value IN (Kalrez; perfluoroelastomer; perfluoro) THEN write \"FFKM\"\nIF value IN (EPR; ethylene propylene) THEN write \"EPDM\"\nIF value IN (silicone; Si) THEN write \"VMQ\"\nIF value IN (Aflas; TFE/P) THEN write \"FEPM\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ORG-5 hardness\nIF value in duro, A, Sh A, Shore A or IRHD THEN write {n} Shore A (IRHD treated as equal)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "ORG-6 aed_resistant\nIF value mentions RGD resistant, AED, ED, NORSOK M-710 or ISO 23936-2 THEN Yes"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Before → after"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "BEFORE",
        "AFTER"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "Size: 2-214": "size_reference: AS568-214"
        },
        {
          "Dash No: 214": "size_reference: AS568-214"
        },
        {
          "ID: 0.984 in": "inner_diameter: 24.99 mm"
        },
        {
          "Cross Section: 0.139\"": "cross_section: 3.53 mm"
        },
        {
          "CS: 3,53": "cross_section: 3.53 mm"
        },
        {
          "Material: Viton": "material: FKM"
        },
        {
          "Compound: Buna-N": "material: NBR"
        },
        {
          "Material: silicone": "material: VMQ"
        },
        {
          "Hardness: 70 duro": "hardness: 70 Shore A"
        },
        {
          "Hardness: 90 IRHD": "hardness: 90 Shore A"
        },
        {
          "RGD: NORSOK M-710": "aed_resistant: Yes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Pro tip. Two decimals for O-rings is deliberate: AS568 sizes differ by as little as 0.08 mm, and rounding to one decimal merges different rings."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "V-Belt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "V-belts come in classical (A, B, C, D), narrow wedge (SPZ, SPA, SPB, SPC) and US narrow (3V, 5V, 8V) sections. The section plus the datum length is the whole identity of the belt."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Write the category as: V-Belt  You may receive: V Belt; Vee Belt; Wedge Belt; Drive Belt; Fan Belt"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Fields at a glance"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Rule",
        "Field key",
        "Labels you may see",
        "What to write"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "VBT-1": "belt_section",
          "Section; Profile; Belt Section": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "VBT-2": "datum_length",
          "Length; Datum Length; Ld; Pitch Length": "{n} mm (whole number)"
        },
        {
          "VBT-3": "construction",
          "Type; Construction; Belt Type": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "VBT-4": "matched_set_qty",
          "Set; Matched Set; Qty in Set": "{n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Rule cards"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "VBT-1 belt_section\nIF value IN (13x8; 13 x 8 mm) THEN write \"A\"\nIF value IN (17x11; 17 x 11 mm) THEN write \"B\"\nIF value IN (22x14) THEN write \"C\"\nIF value IN (32x19) THEN write \"D\"\nIF value IN (spz) THEN write \"SPZ\"\nIF value IN (spa) THEN write \"SPA\"\nIF value IN (spb) THEN write \"SPB\"\nIF value IN (spc) THEN write \"SPC\"\nIF value IN (XPZ; cogged SPZ) THEN write \"XPZ\"\nIF value IN (XPA) THEN write \"XPA\"\nIF value IN (XPB) THEN write \"XPB\"\nIF value IN (3V; 9N) THEN write \"3V\"\nIF value IN (5V; 15N) THEN write \"5V\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "VBT-2 datum_length\nREMOVE Ld, Lw, Lp prefixes\nIF value looks like A42, B75 (classical, inside length in inches) THEN datum = inches x 25.4 + offset\n(A +30, B +40, C +58, D +75 mm)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "VBT-3 construction\nIF value IN (wrapped; classical wrapped; envelope) THEN write \"Wrapped\"\nIF value IN (cogged; notched; raw edge; XP) THEN write \"Raw Edge Cogged\"\nIF value IN (power band; banded; joined; multi-belt) THEN write \"Banded\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "VBT-4 matched_set_qty\nKeep only the number: set of 4 -> 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    }
  ]
}

