{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Hex Bolt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Hex bolts look simple until you meet DIN, ISO, SAE and ASTM in the same spreadsheet. The thread and the grade are the two fields people get wrong."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Write the category as: Hex Bolt  You may receive: Bolt; Hex Bolt; Hex Head Bolt; Hex Cap Screw; HHB"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Fields at a glance"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Rule",
        "Field key",
        "Labels you may see",
        "What to write"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "BLT-1": "thread",
          "Size; Thread; Thread Size; Dia": "M{d}{x{pitch}} | {frac}-{t}pi} UNC/UNF"
        },
        {
          "BLT-2": "length",
          "Length; L; Bolt Length": "{n} mm"
        },
        {
          "BLT-3": "strength_grade",
          "Grade; Property Class; Class; Strength": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "BLT-4": "standard",
          "Standard; Spec; Norm": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "BLT-5": "finish",
          "Finish; Coating; Surface": "Picklist value"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Rule cards"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "BLT-1 thread"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF metric with coarse pitch (M16 x 2.0, M12x1.75) THEN drop the pitch: M16\nIF metric with fine pitch THEN keep it: M16x1.5\nIF inch fraction without TPI THEN add the UNC TPI from the table on page 20: 5/8\" UNC -> 5/8-11 UNC\nIF inch with TPI but no series THEN assume UNC: 1/2-13 -> 1/2-13 UNC"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "BLT-2 length"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "inch x 25.4, one decimal"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "BLT-3 strength_grade"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (8.8; cl 8.8; class 8.8) THEN write \"8.8\"\nIF value IN (10.9; 10.9 class) THEN write \"10.9\"\nIF value IN (12.9) THEN write \"12.9\"\nIF value IN (A2 70; 304 SS 70) THEN write \"A2-70\"\nIF value IN (A4 80; 316 SS 80) THEN write \"A4-80\"\nIF value IN (Gr5; grade 5) THEN write \"SAE Grade 5\"\nIF value IN (Gr8; grade 8) THEN write \"SAE Grade 8\"\nIF value IN (A325) THEN write \"ASTM A325\"\nIF value IN (A490) THEN write \"ASTM A490\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "BLT-4 standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (DIN 931; part thread; partially threaded) THEN write \"ISO 4014\"\nIF value IN (DIN 933; fully threaded; full thread) THEN write \"ISO 4017\"\nIF value IN (ANSI B18.2.1; B18.2.1) THEN write \"ASME B18.2.1\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "BLT-5 finish"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "IF value IN (self colour; plain; black) THEN write \"Plain\"\nIF value IN (BZP; ZP; electro-galvanized; zinc plated) THEN write \"Zinc Plated\"\nIF value IN (HDG; galvanised; hot dip) THEN write \"Hot-Dip Galvanized\"\nIF value IN (zinc flake) THEN write \"Zinc Flake\"\nIF value IN (black oxide) THEN write \"Black Oxide\"\nIF value IN (PTFE; Xylan; fluoropolymer) THEN write \"PTFE Coated\""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    }
  ]
}

