    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Hydraulic Hose"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Hydraulic hose is identified by construction standard and dash size. Similar-looking standards (R2AT and 2SN) are close cousins, not twins - don't convert one into the other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Write the category as: Hydraulic Hose  You may receive: Hose; Hydraulic Hose; Hose Assembly; Hyd Hose"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Fields at a glance"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "",
      "columns": [
        "Rule",
        "Field key",
        "Labels you may see",
        "What to write"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "HSE-1": "hose_standard",
          "Standard; Spec; Type; Hose Type": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "HSE-2": "dash_size",
          "Size; ID; Hose Size; Dash Size": "{n}"
        },
        {
          "HSE-3": "max_working_pressure",
          "WP; Pressure; Working Pressure; MAWP": "{n} bar (whole number)"
        },
        {
          "HSE-4": "end_fitting",
          "Fitting; End Fitting; Ends; Coupling": "Picklist value"
        },
        {
          "HSE-5": "assembly_length",
          "Length; Assembly Length; OAL": "{n} mm (whole number)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Rule cards"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "HSE-1 hose_standard\nIF value IN (R1AT; R1) THEN write \"SAE 100R1AT\"\nIF value IN (R2AT; R2) THEN write \"SAE 100R2AT\"\nIF value IN (1SN) THEN write \"EN 853 1SN\"\nIF value IN (2SN) THEN write \"EN 853 2SN\"\nIF value IN (4SP) THEN write \"EN 856 4SP\"\nIF value IN (4SH) THEN write \"EN 856 4SH\"\nIF value IN (R13) THEN write \"SAE 100R13\"\n\nWatch out! R2AT and 2SN are not the same standard. Translate what is written; never swap one for the other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "HSE-2 dash_size\nLook up inch, mm or DN in the dash-size table (page 20): 1/2 in, 12.7 mm, DN12, #8 -> -8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "HSE-3 max_working_pressure\npsi x 0.0689476, MPa x 10, round to whole bar"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    }
