{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "FAQ"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. The value is right but in the wrong field. Can I move it?\nA. No (GR8). Translate what is in the row. If 'EP2' arrives in the nlgi_grade field, write NLGI 2 there; whoever sends ep_additive separately will get Yes on that row."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. The supplier wrote both units: '50.8 mm (2 in)'. Which do I keep?\nA. The metric number only, tidied per GR4: 50.8 mm."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. Why 'CHECK:' and not just leaving it?\nA. Because a CHECK: row is searchable. Reviewers filter on it every morning; a silently kept value is never looked at again."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. A brand name is the only thing I have (Viton, Kevlar, Aflas).\nA. Several brand names are listed as accepted inputs and translate to the generic material. If a brand isn't listed, write CHECK: with the brand name."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. Is 'TBD' the same as 'CHECK:'?\nA. No. TBD means nobody told us. CHECK: means somebody told us something we can't translate."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. Can I write 25.0 mm to show precision?\nA. Not for normal fields (GR4 drops trailing zeros). O-ring dimensions are the exception: always two decimals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. The category is spelled 'Oring' / 'O Ring' / 'o-ring'.\nA. All the same: write O-Ring (GR1). Watch the capital R."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. Should I correct R2AT to 2SN because they're 'the same hose'?\nA. Never. They're similar, not identical (see chapter 8)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. Old cut level '5' - isn't that roughly Cut D?\nA. Roughly isn't good enough for PPE. Write CHECK: level 5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Q. Two rows describe the same field for the same item with different values.\nA. Translate both as they are. Duplicate detection happens later, not here."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Your end-of-batch checklist"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Check",
      "columns": [
        "Check"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "Check": "[] Every Item is a category name from a chapter title, Title Case."
        },
        {
          "Check": "[] Every Attribute is a lower_snake_case field key from that chapter."
        },
        {
          "Check": "[] Picklist values match the guide exactly - capitals, spaces and symbols."
        },
        {
          "Check": "[] Numbers have one space before the unit and no trailing zeros (O-rings: two decimals)."
        },
        {
          "Check": "[] No inches, psi, gallons, pounds or ounces left anywhere."
        },
        {
          "Check": "[] Missing values say TBD; untranslatable values start with CHECK: and keep the original text."
        },
        {
          "Check": "[] Row count and row order are unchanged."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sample field guide for testing data standardization. Keep it on your desk, not in a drawer."
    }
  ]
}

